<title>CANADA: Placer Dome sees US$11 million gain.</title>
<headline>Placer Dome sees US$11 million gain.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Placer Dome Inc said on Tuesday it expected an after-tax gain of about US$11 million on the sale of its 30.8 percent stake in Gibraltar Mines Ltd to Westmin Resources Ltd.</p>
<p>Westmin is bidding C$8.85 a share in cash and stock for Gibraltar for a total value of C$307 million.</p>
<p>Gibraltar is a copper company. Placer, which focuses on gold mining, announced last week it intended to sell its stake in Gibraltar because it was not a core asset.</p>
</text>
